# Miner Llama v4 preset: Ornith-1.5-122B, Ornith-1.5-122B Pascal N2P GGUF (valid1: N2P/N3P experts, Q5_0 output layer)
# on nine P106-090 cards, 49,152-token context.
# Build: v4-rc2 (pascal-p106-v4 eb82916d3, upstream b12360 merged). On it this file loads with the same memory on
# every card and gives the same greedy replies as before the upstream merge (docs/data/2026-11-13_c831_upstream/,
# part 3). Its agent check against v3.0 is the release test in README.md; v3.0 on this file and line: 16.3 tok/s,
# 12/12, and 16.42 tok/s, 12/12, on a second rig (docs/data/2026-11-05_release_regression/,
# docs/data/2026-11-06_ornith_mtp_rig2/).
# This is v3.0's line (release/ornith-v3/settings.env) with the v4 switches that act on Ornith's path (qwen35moe, a
# hybrid of 36 Gated DeltaNet and 12 attention layers): host-side, exact (the same tokens), and checked on nine P106
# cards. The file holds N2P, N3P, Q5_0 and Q8_0 weights and F32 routers; Ornith runs without a draft, so it decodes
# one token a step and the v4 kernels of 2-8-token verify passes never run here (README.md, "What v4 changes").
# Use: . settings.env && env $PRESET_ENV llama-server -m "$MODELS/$PRESET_MODEL" $PRESET_ARGS --host 127.0.0.1 --port 8080
PRESET_MODEL=Ornith-1.5-122B-N2P-N3P-valid1-headQ5_0.gguf

PRESET_ENV=
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_KEEPALIVE=decode"  # v3.0's: a one-thread block per card holds the boost clock while a split decodes; 16.3 against 14.9 tok/s (Q1021, Q1045)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV GGML_CUDA_KEEPALIVE_EAGER=1"  # the keep-alive block ends before a kernel's first launch on a card, so the launch does not wait ~1 s for it; a 2,760-token prompt 24,712.63 and 24,744.13 ms against 26,637.95 and 26,065.24 without (C811, C817, Q1417, Q1426; R140, on Flash-Next)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SERVER_YIELD=2"  # a step's yield to the server's reader thread wakes it only when a read waits, the same replies (C741, Q1310; R122)
PRESET_ENV="$PRESET_ENV LLAMA_SAMPLING_TOP_K_ROWS=1"  # the card's sampling chain (-bs, top-k 20) runs one top-k over its output rows and reads the logits unpadded, the same tokens (C691, Q1223; R83; the graph fixed by C802, Q1406)
PRESET_ENV=${PRESET_ENV# }

# v3.0's line, unchanged; every flag is explained in release/ornith-v3/README.md:
PRESET_ARGS="-ngl 99 -fa on -c 49152 -np 1 -bs --ctx-checkpoints 4 --cache-ram 0 --jinja --reasoning-format deepseek --temp 0.6 --top-p 0.95 --top-k 20 --min-p 0 -b 2048 -ub 512 -ts 6,6,6,6,5,5,5,5,6 -fit off"
